CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*std::optional<std::tag-pair<signed_int,signed_int>>::optional\(this,(ref|rref).*$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct optional'.*$
^.*address_of error.*not an lvalue.*$
--
Regression for converting a function-template call's prvalue result
(std::make_pair with a materialized-temporary argument) into a
std::optional via its converting constructor.  See main.cpp for the
[conv.rval]/[class.temporary] grounding: a materialized temporary is
a glvalue whose address may be taken, so re-typechecking an
already-typechecked call carrying `address_of(temporary_object(...))`
must succeed.  Verified at the goto-program level (full
std::optional<std::pair> BMC exceeds symex memory limits).
